+# Research — real meeting terminal finalization bridge
+
+Issue: `ce942338-35af-4960-ae83-ebc55bdbbe2a`  
+Baseline: `origin/main` at `42e30d88bc516dc6472c9f1bb837bd694844aa47`  
+Date: 2026-08-08
+
+## Finding
+
+The defect is confirmed. The local browser stop path waits for `MediaRecorder.stop()` and then
+writes `status: "completed"` (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:671-680`). The meeting API triggers an
+explicit final materialization only for `status == "stopped"`
+(`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:2838-2871`), and the shared terminal predicate also recognizes
+only `stopped` (`apps/meeting-api/backend/workflows/meeting_state_update.py:18-19`). A completed
+meeting therefore does not finalize its last partial chapter at stop time.
+
+The visible artifact surface and the legacy summary API are also split:
+
+- `useMeetingState` loads state, chapters, decisions, action items, questions, and recent lines
+  (`apps/meeting-web/src/hooks/useMeetingState.js:128-205`); `MeetingSummaryBlock` renders those
+  artifacts (`packages/ui-meeting/src/meeting-summary-block.jsx:154-182,298-308`).
+- `App` separately fetches `GET /summary` but stores it in a state setter whose value is never read
+  (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:149,287-315`).
+- `GET /summary` reads the separate `summaries` table
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:3130-3141`), while transcript chunk and terminal
+  materialization write `meeting_state`, `chapter_summaries`, and generated records
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:2064-2230`).
+
+The existing platform E2E explicitly starts downstream of the broken bridge by directly seeding a
+generated `action_items` row (`apps/platform-web/e2e/meeting-loop.spec.ts:13-25` and
+`apps/platform-web/e2e/db-provenance.e2e.ts:50-115`). It proves proposal acceptance, not transcript
+finalization.
+
+## Current data and event flow
+
+1. `useAudioRecorder` emits a browser chunk; `App.handleChunkReady` sends it through
+   `POST /meetings/{meeting_id}/transcribe` (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:356-385`).
+2. The API stores transcript segments and updates meeting duration/count
+   (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:2886-2994`). Boundary crossings may invoke non-final
+   materialization.
+3. The UI refreshes the summary-first surface after a chunk through
+   `syncSummaryStateAfterTranscriptionChunk` (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:367-377`).
+4. User Stop awaits the recorder, then writes `completed` (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:671-682`).
+5. The API persists that status but does not call final materialization because it checks only
+   `stopped` (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:2867-2871`).
+6. Read-time repair checks the same `stopped` predicate. `completed` returns false, so state and
+   chapter reads do not repair the missing final window
+   (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1992-2023,3144-3161,3181-3198`).
+
+## Existing behavior worth preserving
+
+- Materialization reads all ordered transcript segments, replaces tenant-scoped derived state and
+  chapters, and commits them together (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:2071-2224`).
+- Chapter and generated-record IDs are content/window-derived, so replacement can be deterministic
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1931-1949`; `apps/meeting-api/backend/services/chapter_summary.py:207-250`).
+- Exact-boundary and cross-chapter dedup behavior already has focused tests
+  (`apps/meeting-api/tests/backend/test_summary_routes.py:472-616`).
+- Existing fixtures cover several stopped meetings, but none uses `completed`
+  (`apps/meeting-api/tests/backend/fixtures/*.json`).
+- The current explicit-stop test proves only `stopped -> one materialize call`
+  (`apps/meeting-api/tests/backend/test_summary_routes.py:789-836`).
+
+## Edge-case gaps
+
+- Empty transcript: final chapter builder returns no chapters
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1881-1888`). This should be a successful empty finalization,
+  not an exception or a fabricated summary.
+- Short meeting: the final partial window can be dropped by the sparse-window threshold
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1923-1927`). Finalization must not lose the only meaningful
+  transcript in a short meeting.
+- Duplicate/reconnect: `record_completed_job` always inserts a new random job row
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1686-1728`); its current use is observability, not an
+  exactly-once claim.
+- Failure after status persistence: the route writes the terminal status before materialization.
+  It has no durable finalization state, transcript watermark, or retry contract.
+- Inactivity: read-time logic treats stale `recording` as finalizable based only on `updated_at`
+  (`apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py:1992-2004`). Silence alone cannot prove the local recorder or
+  durable upload drain has ended.
+- Consent: the shipped local path checks microphone permission and exposes Recording/Paused/Stop
+  controls (`apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx:618-633`;
+  `packages/ui-meeting/src/meeting-summary-block.jsx:249-295`), but no persisted consent artifact is
+  present in the inspected code. This plan preserves the indicator and consumes the local-capture
+  consent/durability contract; it does not invent legal consent semantics.
+
+## Recommended pattern
+
+Use a dedicated finalization command and durable ledger keyed by the acknowledged transcript
+watermark. Canonical stored terminal status is `completed`; incoming legacy `stopped` is accepted,
+normalized to `completed`, and reported through compatibility telemetry. The command performs one
+transactional artifact replacement/upsert and records success against the watermark. Duplicate
+terminal events return the stored result. Failed attempts can retry the same key; a later transcript
+watermark creates a new repair attempt only when the capture durability contract proves those
+segments were acknowledged.
+
+The finalizer must depend on:
+
+1. caller-authority PR A for meeting/derivative visibility and provenance contracts;
+2. caller-authority PR B for the meeting-owned action-candidate write seam and review boundary;
+3. local durability issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a` for capture-session sequence and
+   contiguous-ack evidence.
+
+It must not own PR B's candidate schema, Add/Adjust/Dismiss behavior, promotion, or review UI.
+
+## Security and reliability pass
+
+| Area | Applies | Plan response |
+|---|---|---|
+| A01 broken access control | Yes | Reuse caller PR A visibility/provenance check before transcript read or artifact write; missing authority denies. |
+| A02 crypto | No new primitive | Never copy raw audio/transcript into logs or ledger metadata. |
+| A03 injection | Yes | Parameterized SQL only; status and terminal reason are closed enums; transcript remains data. |
+| A04 insecure design | Yes | Durable idempotency key, transactional writes, explicit incomplete-capture conflict, fail-closed authority. |
+| A05 misconfiguration | Yes | Feature flag the new endpoint/legacy alias; reject unknown terminal states. |
+| A06 vulnerable components | No | No dependency is required. |
+| A07 authentication | Yes | Existing authenticated actor plus caller PR A authorization. |
+| A08 integrity | Yes | Watermark binds capture session, last contiguous sequence, segment count, and final timestamp. |
+| A09 logging | Yes | Structured IDs/counts/timing only; no transcript text, participant names, or audio. |
+| A10 SSRF | No | No provider or URL fetch is added. |
+
+## Baseline and coordination evidence
+
+- Worktree is a clean exact fork of `origin/main` at `42e30d88bc516dc6472c9f1bb837bd694844aa47`.
+- Conflict detection reports the issue is not yet in the file index; merge simulation reports no
+  conflict with main.
+- The merge-order helper reports a pre-existing dependency cycle, and stale-worktree output names
+  unrelated old worktrees. No override or mutation was made.
+- `forge team verify` reports a pre-existing missing team-map identity and GitHub issues #145/#141
+  not imported. The distinct Kernel actor lease is independently proven.
+- `forge research` is unavailable in this installed CLI; this file supplies the required research
+  artifact using the repository's live code as primary evidence.
+- Untouched baseline validation passed: meeting API `226 passed, 1 skipped` and meeting-web
+  `27 files / 132 tests passed`. The first web run could not find Vitest because the isolated
+  worktree had no dependencies; `bun install --frozen-lockfile` made no lockfile changes, after which
+  the suite passed.
